`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The project enforces `DeckentError` over generic `Error` in `src/core/` via a lint script (`check-error-handling.mjs`) that is itself tested in `tests/core/error-handling-unification.test.ts`. This creates a virtuous cycle: new code in `src/core/` that violates the convention is caught automatically in CI, not just during code review. The `throw new DeckentError('E_PROVIDER_HTTP_ERROR', ...)` calls here are caught internally by the `try/catch` in `refreshProvider()` and converted to a `RefreshResult.error` string — meaning they never escape to the caller as typed errors, but the convention still applies because the lint rule covers all `throw new Error` in the directory.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

